      "source": [
        "# Appliances Energy Prediction — Deep Learning for Time Series (Course Project)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Task:** forecast household appliance energy use (`Appliances`, Wh per 10 min) with a naive baseline, a linear reference, an **MLP**, and a **1D-CNN**, under a leakage-free, chronological protocol.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Design decisions\n",
        "| Item | Choice | Why |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Target | `Appliances` (Wh per 10-min interval) | Course dataset target |\n",
        "| Frequency | Native 10 min, **no resampling** | Data is already perfectly regular; resampling would discard information |\n",
        "| Horizon | **H = 1 step** (predict the next 10 min); `HORIZON` is a config variable | Single-step is the cleanest fair comparison |\n",
        "| Split | Chronological **60 / 20 / 20** by row index, no shuffling across time | Course requirement |\n",
        "| Inputs | Past `Appliances` + **lagged** sensor/weather readings (window ends at t, target is t+H) + **future-known calendar** features for the target time | Observed weather is only used as lagged input; no forecasts exist in the data, so no future weather is assumed |\n",
        "| Dropped features | `rv1`, `rv2` (random noise by the dataset description; verified on training data only) | Feature-selection decision justified on train only |\n",
        "| Loss | Huber (δ = 1) on the standardised target | Target is spiky/right-skewed; robust to outliers |\n",
        "| Baseline | Naive (last value) = primary baseline; seasonal-naive (same time yesterday) and Ridge as extra references | Naive is the required non-neural baseline |\n",
        "| HPO | Grid search, scored on **validation only** (seed 42); test set untouched until the end | Course requirement |\n",
        "| Final runs | Best config per model, retrained with 5 seeds, mean ± std on test | Quantifies seed noise |"
      ]
    },
    {
