      "source": [
        "## 4. Preprocessing, features and window shapes\n",
        "* **Imputer** (median) and **StandardScaler** are fitted on training rows `[0, n_train)` only, then applied to all rows. (The data has no missing values, so the imputer is a no-op, but it is kept in the pipeline for correctness.)\n",
        "* The **target scaler** is fitted separately on training `Appliances`; predictions are inverse-transformed back to Wh for all metrics.\n",
        "* **Calendar features** are deterministic functions of the timestamp (hour and weekday as sin/cos, weekend flag), so they need no fitting and are legitimately known in the future. The calendar vector of the **target time** is appended to every time step of the window.\n",
        "* **Window:** inputs = rows `[t−L+1 … t]`, target = `Appliances[t+H]`."
      ]
    },
